**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Food Delivery & Dish Retrieval**

---

### 1. Goal Tables

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Target Condition / Enquired Info | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------------------------------|----------|---------------|
| **G1 – Deliver Food to Inpatient Room** | Deliver food from the kitchen to the requested inpatient room. | **FALLBACK(G4, G5)** | Achieve | “Food successfully delivered to the inpatient room and either placed on the table or retrieved by the patient.” | OR | The mission offers two mutually exclusive delivery modes – hand‑over to the patient or direct table delivery – so a fallback is required. |
| **G2 – Query Patient Retrieval Capability** | Obtain information on whether the patient can retrieve food from the robot’s tray. | – | Query | “PatientRetrievalCapability (Yes/No/Unknown)” | – | The robot needs this knowledge to decide whether hand‑over is feasible. |
| **G4 – Perform Hand‑Over** | Hand‑over food to the patient, requiring patient retrieval and door opening. | **AND** | Perform | – | AND | Hand‑over succeeds only if the patient can retrieve the meal **and** the door is open, so all sub‑tasks must succeed. |
| **G5 – Perform Direct Delivery** | Deliver food directly to the room table. | **AND** | Perform | – | AND | All steps (pickup, transport, table placement) must be completed. |
| **G6 – Retrieve Dirty Dishes** | Retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room. | **FALLBACK(AT7, AT8, AT9)** | Perform | – | OR | The robot can retrieve dishes alone, with another robot, or with human help – a fallback between the three options. |
| **G7 – Open Room Door** | Open the room door to allow robot entry or exit. | **FALLBACK(AT10, AT11, AT12)** | Perform | – | OR | The door can be opened by the robot alone, by the robot + human, or by two robots. |

---

### 2. Task Tables

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1 – Indicate Meal to Patient** | Robot tells the patient which meal to retrieve from its tray. | AND | Room | 1 | One robot can communicate the meal identity. |
| **AT2 – Wait for Patient to Retrieve Meal** | Robot waits until the patient picks up the indicated meal. | AND | Room | 1 | Waiting is required to ensure the patient actually retrieves the meal. |
| **AT3 – Verify Correct Meal Retrieved** | Robot checks that the patient has taken the correct meal. | AND | Room | 1 | Verification prevents wrong‑meal delivery. |
| **AT4 – Pick Up Meal from Kitchen** | Robot picks up the requested meal(s) from the kitchen. | AND | Kitchen | 1 | One robot can carry the meal. |
| **AT5 – Transport Meal to Room** | Robot carries the meal from kitchen to the inpatient room. | AND | Hallway → Room | 1 | Direct transport is needed. |
| **AT6 – Deliver Meal to Table** | Robot places the meal onto the room table using special manipulation skills. | AND | Room Table | 1 | Special manipulation is required for table placement. |
| **AT7 – Retrieve Dishes Unassisted** | Robot retrieves dirty dishes from the room without assistance. | AND | Room | 1 | Some dishes are light enough for a single robot. |
| **AT8 – Retrieve Dishes with Two Robots** | Two robots cooperate to retrieve dirty dishes from the room. | AND | Room | [2,2] | Heavy dishes may need two robots. |
| **AT9 – Retrieve Dishes with Human** | Robot retrieves dirty dishes with assistance from a human. | AND | Room | 1 | Human helps lift heavy dishes; robot still required. |
| **AT10 – Open Door by Robot** | Robot opens the room door alone. | AND | Room Door | 1 | Possible when door is simple or unlocked. |
| **AT11 – Open Door with Human** | Robot opens the room door with help from a human. | AND | Room Door | 1 | Human assists if door is locked or heavy. |
| **AT12 – Open Door with Robot** | Two robots cooperate to open the room door. | AND | Room Door | [2,2] | Some doors require two robots to push. |
| **AT13 – Monitor Meal Retrieval** | Robot monitors the room to detect when the patient retrieves the meal. | AND | Room | 1 | Continuous monitoring is needed to log the event. |
| **AT14 – Alert Wrong Meal** | Robot alerts staff if the patient retrieves an incorrect meal. | AND | Room | 1 | Immediate notification avoids confusion. |
| **AT15 – Receive Dish Retrieval Request** | Robot receives a request from the patient to retrieve dishes. | AND | Room | 1 | The robot must listen to the request before starting dish retrieval. |

